Glassline is an unofficial port of Mirror's Edge (iPad) to PC and Android. Its
source code (the "Software") is published so that it can be read, studied,
built and played with your own copy of the game, and improved by way of
contributions to the original project - the repository in which the copyright
holders publish the Software. The Software is not free or open source software:
every right that is not expressly granted below is reserved.

1. What this license covers

   a) This license covers only the work of the copyright holders: the port and
      its launcher, the build scripts, the port's own texts and images, and
      the changes and additions the copyright holders made to the game code.

   b) Mirror's Edge, its code, its resources (graphics, models, sound, music,
      texts, levels) and its name and logo belong to Electronic Arts Inc. and
      its licensors. The code in src/ and include/ was reconstructed from the
      game; no right to it, or to anything else of Electronic Arts, is granted
      by this license or by the copyright holders. No game resources are
      included in the Software: the Software loads them from a copy of the
      game that you supply yourself.

   c) Third-party components (port/third_party/ and the libraries the build
      downloads or bundles) are covered by their own licenses, which are
      shipped with them.

